# Keeps the compiled tests out of the published tarball. `prepublishOnly`
# copies this file to dist/src/.npmignore; it is never used from here.
#
# It HAS to be nested inside dist/src. Do not "simplify" it, because the two
# tidier-looking spellings both ship the tests without saying so:
#
#   - A negated `files` entry ("!dist/src/**/*.test.js"): npm honours it, pnpm
#     ignores it outright. With it in place, `pnpm publish --dry-run` still
#     lists every test file. This package publishes with the pnpm pinned in
#     `packageManager`, so that spelling is a silent no-op.
#   - A .npmignore at the repo root: ignored by BOTH npm and pnpm as soon as
#     `files` exists in package.json, because `files` wins.
#
# Only a .npmignore INSIDE an included directory is honoured by both packers.
# It strips these artifacts at every depth, and excludes itself from the
# tarball too.
#
# If you change this, verify with `npm pack` AND `pnpm pack` and diff the file
# lists. Reading the config is not enough -- that is exactly how the two
# spellings above look correct while shipping 84 test files.
*.test.js
*.test.d.ts
*.test.js.map
*.test.d.ts.map
